# command-process

Inputs:

- command-wait output: `{{ upstream["command-wait"].task_path }}` (fields
  `kind`, `command`, `slug`); `kind` is always `action` when this task runs.
- workdir: `{{ run.workdir }}`
- notepad: `{{ run.workdir }}/notepad.md`

## Task

Set the tiling activity to the slug throughout:

```bash
~/.kiro/skills/home/tiling/scripts/run-ttm.sh activity set "notepad(<slug>)"
```

Then:

1. Compute `NN` as the next one-based, zero-padded index across the existing
   `NN-*` sub-folders of the workdir.
2. `mkdir "{{ run.workdir }}/${NN}-<slug>"`.
3. Write the verbatim `command` to `${NN}-<slug>/request.md`.
4. Do all intermediate work under `${NN}-<slug>/`.
5. Append a `## <slug>` sub-section to `{{ run.workdir }}/notepad.md`: one
   paragraph with the verbatim `command`, one paragraph describing the
   outcome.

## Output

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loom/scripts/loom.sh
$LOOM output init "{{ run.workdir }}" --task command-process
$LOOM output add  "{{ run.workdir }}" --task command-process \
    --set kind=action \
    --set action_dir="{{ run.workdir }}/${NN}-<slug>" \
    --set outcome='<short description>'
```
